requires — Declares that an interface depends on other interfaces.

Syntax:
  interface Named {
    name: string
  }
  interface Aged {
    age: int
  }
  interface HasKey {
    type Key
    key: Self.Key
  }
  interface Person requires Named, Aged, HasKey<Key = string> {
    function introduce(self) -> string
  }

`requires` is interface composition, not inheritance. Required interfaces may include associated type bindings, as in `requires HasKey<Key = string>`. Implementors of a required interface must also implement the required parent interfaces; cycles are rejected. Use `requires`, not `extends`, between interfaces.
